From: Redmi 9 mainline port <lancelot@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] power: supply: generic-adc-battery: Do not report charging without a charger

power_supply_am_i_supplied() returns a negative errno, -ENODEV, when
no charger power-supply is registered at all. The negative value is
not zero, so the driver takes it as "supplied" and permanently reports
POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING on systems where the battery is the only
power-supply device.

Treat any non-positive return value as not supplied.
---
 drivers/power/supply/generic-adc-battery.c

--- a/drivers/power/supply/generic-adc-battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/generic-adc-battery.c
@@ -130,7 +130,12 @@
 	adc_bat = container_of(delayed_work, struct gab, bat_work);
 	status = adc_bat->status;
 
-	if (!power_supply_am_i_supplied(adc_bat->psy))
+	/*
+	 * power_supply_am_i_supplied() returns -ENODEV when there is no
+	 * charger power-supply at all, which must not be mistaken for
+	 * "supplied": without a charger to ask, the battery is discharging.
+	 */
+	if (power_supply_am_i_supplied(adc_bat->psy) <= 0)
 		adc_bat->status =  POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 	else if (gab_charge_finished(adc_bat))
 		adc_bat->status = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
